# --- from the standard Node template, the parts that apply here ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Secrets. Change 1b's host identity is a secret today; change 7a adds more.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS junk. Development is on Windows, change 6 runs on Linux.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- this project ---

# Build output — esbuild regenerates these from `public/`. Tracking them means
# every source edit shows twice in the diff, once as cause and once as effect.
*.bundle.js
*.bundle.js.map

# Generated media — `npm run content` in step0/ rebuilds it (~2.3 GB, 1800
# fMP4 segments of synthetic testsrc2).
step0/content/

# Scratch from the spike rig's runs.
spike-host-origin/.tmp/

# Session handoff notes — transient by construction; the durable record is the
# change's artifacts.
.claude/temp/

# IDE workspace state. Per-machine and per-developer — module paths, code-style
# defaults, VCS mappings — and it carries none of the project's reasoning.
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   *.md anywhere — the docs are the review surface. Session D3 edits them, and
#     they are inside the diff it reviews. An untracked doc is the one thing a
#     subtractive review cannot undo.
#   step0/results/, spike-host-origin/results/ — measurement records, not build
#     output. They are the evidence behind FINDINGS.md and RESULT.md.
#   package-lock.json — the hls.js version is load-bearing (PLAN.md, change 7a).
